#
#  The TNG soundtrack, declared as a music bank.
#
#  A `@media/music` label names a BANK - a folder holding start/main/victory/failure.ogg
#  plus low/ medium/ high/ - not a track. `music_get_list()` finds this, so it appears in
#  the server console's Music dropdown for any mission that loads this add-on, and
#  `MUSIC_SELECT: TNG_Music` (or the display name) selects it.
#
#  WHERE THE FILES ARE, and why this may play the stock music for now. The bank travels in
#  this mod's shared-media pack at `media/music/TNG_Music`, beside the rest of the art,
#  which is where sbs_utils looks. The ENGINE is the problem: `set_music_folder` accepts a
#  bare name under `data/audio/music` and HANGS on anything else - not an error, the call
#  never returns (measured in `missions/music_probe`, engine 1.3.6). So sbs_utils resolves
#  the bank, declines to hand the engine a path, logs a warning naming the folder it found,
#  and plays `default`.
#
#  Nothing here changes when that is fixed: flip MUSIC_ENGINE_ACCEPTS_PATHS and this bank
#  plays from the pack. A player who wants it today copies the folder into
#  `data/audio/music/TNG_Music`, which the resolver checks first.
#
@media/music/TNG_Music "TNG Music"


#
#  The TNG skyboxes.
#
#  A `@media/skybox` label only REGISTERS a name at compile time; something has to schedule
#  it. LegendaryMissions' server console does that once at the lobby with
#  `skybox_schedule_random()`, so every label here joins that random pick, and a map or a
#  console can override per ship or per client via the `skybox` inventory value.
#
#  UNLIKE MUSIC, THE SKYBOX PATH IS UNRESTRICTED. `set_sky_box` takes a real path in any
#  spelling, so these load straight out of this mod's shared-media pack at
#  `media/skybox/<name>.png` with nothing copied into `data/graphics`. The segfault-on-a-
#  path trap is music's alone.
#
#  THE ONE SILENT FAILURE: a label whose PNG is missing is dropped from the random pick
#  without a word - the symptom is "the new skies never come up". That happens if a
#  consuming mission forgets the `shared_media` line in its story.json, so check that first
#  if these never appear.
#
#  The art is generated, not painted - `_tools/gen_skybox_tng.py` builds each one as a 4x3
#  cube cross where every pixel is a pure function of its 3D direction, which is what makes
#  the twelve cube edges seamless by construction rather than by repair.
#
@media/skybox/tng_deep "TNG Deep Space"
@media/skybox/tng_klingon_border "Klingon Border"
@media/skybox/tng_bajor "Bajoran System"
@media/skybox/tng_neutral_zone "Romulan Neutral Zone"
@media/skybox/tng_delta "Delta Quadrant"
@media/skybox/tng_wolf359 "Wolf 359"
